{"title":"Career Roadmap · Cabin Crew","role":"Cabin Crew","summary":"A Cabin Crew professional is responsible for passenger safety, emergency procedures, onboard service, security awareness, communication, and overall passenger experience. Although hospitality skills are valuable, safety is the primary responsibility of cabin crew.","facts":{"Current degree":"BHM / B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration / BTTM","Course":"Airline & Airport Management"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Timeline","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Aviation, communication and service"}],[{"text":"Preparation"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Safety, grooming, fitness and passenger handling"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Aviation operations and interview readiness"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Year 3–4"},{"text":"Cabin Crew Trainee / Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Safety, service and operational competence"}],[{"text":"Experienced"},{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Senior cabin responsibilities"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"5–10 years"},{"text":"Senior Cabin Crew / Purser / Cabin Supervisor"}],[{"text":"Management"},{"text":"8–15 years"},{"text":"Cabin training/quality/operations"}],[{"text":"Senior Leadership"},{"text":"15+ years"},{"text":"Cabin Services / Inflight Operations leadership"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Cabin crew recruitment is driven primarily by the airline's current eligibility, medical, fitness, language, height/reach, grooming, documentation and training requirements. A BHM/BTTM degree can strengthen the profile, but it does not by itself guarantee eligibility or selection."}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Aviation & hospitality foundation"},{"text":"Communication, service, aviation basics"},{"text":"Presentation/certificates"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Cabin crew readiness"},{"text":"Safety, first aid, grooming, passenger handling"},{"text":"Practical training"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Professional readiness"},{"text":"Emergency awareness, service, English, interview skills"},{"text":"Mock interviews + internship"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Employment readiness"},{"text":"Airline-specific preparation, leadership, aviation operations"},{"text":"Cabin crew applications"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Aviation & Hospitality Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Aviation basics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airline industry structure"},{"text":"Airport operations"},{"text":"Aircraft types"},{"text":"Passenger journey"},{"text":"Check-in"},{"text":"Boarding"},{"text":"Baggage"},{"text":"Immigration"},{"text":"Security"},{"text":"Departure/arrival procedures"},{"text":"Domestic vs international aviation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Hospitality"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Guest service"},{"text":"Service etiquette"},{"text":"Complaint handling"},{"text":"Professional communication"},{"text":"Cross-cultural communication"},{"text":"Hospitality psychology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spoken English"},{"text":"Professional vocabulary"},{"text":"Telephone communication"},{"text":"Public speaking"},{"text":"Active listening"},{"text":"Conflict resolution"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Cabin Crew Readiness"},{"type":"h","text":"Safety Fundamentals"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the purpose of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Safety demonstrations"},{"text":"Emergency exits"},{"text":"Emergency lighting"},{"text":"Seat belts"},{"text":"Life jackets"},{"text":"Oxygen systems"},{"text":"Fire extinguishers"},{"text":"Smoke procedures"},{"text":"Evacuation procedures"},{"text":"Turbulence procedures"},{"text":"Cabin decompression awareness"},{"text":"Emergency communication"}]},{"type":"p","text":"You should understand the principles and procedures, while airline-specific operational training is provided by the employer."},{"type":"h","text":"First Aid & Medical Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic first aid"},{"text":"CPR"},{"text":"AED awareness"},{"text":"Fainting"},{"text":"Burns"},{"text":"Minor injuries"},{"text":"Motion sickness"},{"text":"Allergic reactions"},{"text":"Medical emergencies"},{"text":"Passenger distress"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A recognised first-aid/CPR course can be useful, but airline-specific training remains essential."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Cabin Crew Preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Passenger handling"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn how to deal with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nervous passengers"},{"text":"Elderly passengers"},{"text":"Children"},{"text":"Passengers requiring assistance"},{"text":"Language barriers"},{"text":"Difficult passengers"},{"text":"Medical situations"},{"text":"Flight delays"},{"text":"Disruptions"},{"text":"Service complaints"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Service"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Meal service"},{"text":"Beverage service"},{"text":"Cabin presentation"},{"text":"Galley organisation"},{"text":"Service sequencing"},{"text":"Passenger interaction"},{"text":"Special meal awareness"},{"text":"Premium-cabin service concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Grooming & Professional Presentation"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Professional posture"},{"text":"Personal grooming"},{"text":"Uniform etiquette"},{"text":"Professional appearance"},{"text":"Clear speech"},{"text":"Confident body language"},{"text":"Appropriate makeup/grooming where applicable"},{"text":"Professional etiquette"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Airline-specific grooming standards vary, so candidates should check the current official recruitment requirements of each airline."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation Options"},{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Focus","Career Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"Domestic Cabin Crew"},{"text":"Short-haul operations"},{"text":"Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"International Cabin Crew"},{"text":"International routes"},{"text":"International Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"Premium Cabin"},{"text":"Business/First Class"},{"text":"Premium Cabin Specialist"}],[{"text":"Long-Haul"},{"text":"Long-distance operations"},{"text":"Senior Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"Safety/Training"}],[{"text":"Cabin Service"},{"text":"Passenger experience"},{"text":"Service Specialist"}],[{"text":"Cabin Training"},{"text":"Crew development"},{"text":"Cabin Trainer"}],[{"text":"Cabin Quality"},{"text":"Service audits"},{"text":"Quality Executive"}],[{"text":"Aviation Operations"},{"text":"Ground/cabin coordination"},{"text":"Aviation Operations"}],[{"text":"VIP Aviation"},{"text":"Premium/private aviation"},{"text":"VIP Cabin Crew"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships & Practical Exposure","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cabin crew positions generally require airline-specific recruitment and training, so a conventional hotel internship is not a substitute for cabin crew training."},{"type":"p","text":"However, useful exposure can come from:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airlines"},{"text":"Airport passenger-service companies"},{"text":"Airport ground-handling companies"},{"text":"Airline customer-service departments"},{"text":"Hotel front office"},{"text":"Luxury hospitality"},{"text":"Guest relations"},{"text":"Travel companies"},{"text":"Aviation training organisations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful internship roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airport Operations Intern"},{"text":"Passenger Service Intern"},{"text":"Ground Handling Intern"},{"text":"Customer Service Intern"},{"text":"Guest Relations Intern"},{"text":"Airline Operations Intern"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This builds transferable skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Passenger interaction"},{"text":"Boarding processes"},{"text":"Customer service"},{"text":"Airport operations"},{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Disruption handling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong Practical Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Passenger Journey & Cabin Service Simulation\""},{"type":"p","text":"Create a complete simulated passenger journey:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Booking","Airport arrival","Check-in","Security","Boarding","Cabin safety","Meal service","Passenger issue","Turbulence response","Arrival","Disembarkation"]},{"type":"p","text":"Document:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Passenger touchpoints"},{"text":"Safety procedures"},{"text":"Service standards"},{"text":"Communication scripts"},{"text":"Emergency scenarios"},{"text":"Complaint-resolution procedures"},{"text":"Accessibility considerations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates that you understand the cabin crew role beyond appearance and customer service."}]},{"heading":"Certifications and Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"First Aid"},{"text":"CPR"},{"text":"AED awareness"},{"text":"Fire safety"},{"text":"Emergency response"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Aviation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation fundamentals"},{"text":"Airport operations"},{"text":"Cabin crew fundamentals"},{"text":"Passenger handling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Service"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitality service"},{"text":"Customer experience"},{"text":"Cross-cultural communication"},{"text":"Conflict management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Languages"},{"type":"p","text":"An additional language can be valuable for international or specific-market roles."},{"type":"p","text":"Examples:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arabic"},{"text":"French"},{"text":"German"},{"text":"Spanish"},{"text":"Mandarin"},{"text":"Japanese"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The value depends on the airline's route network and recruitment needs."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible entry-level roles include:"},{"type":"table","header":["Role","Level"],"rows":[[{"text":"Cabin Crew Trainee"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Cabin Crew"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Flight Attendant"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Passenger Service Executive"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Ground Staff Executive"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Airport Customer Service Executive"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Airline Guest Service Executive"},{"text":"Entry"}],[{"text":"Airport Operations Executive"},{"text":"Entry"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Cabin Crew Interview Questions"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Why do you want to become cabin crew?"},{"text":"What is the primary responsibility of cabin crew?"},{"text":"Why is safety more important than service?"},{"text":"How would you handle an angry passenger?"},{"text":"How would you handle a passenger who refuses to follow instructions?"},{"text":"What would you do during severe turbulence?"},{"text":"How would you assist an elderly passenger?"},{"text":"How would you handle a medical emergency onboard?"},{"text":"How would you manage a conflict with another crew member?"},{"text":"How would you handle a passenger complaint?"},{"text":"Why is teamwork important in aviation?"},{"text":"How would you deal with cultural differences among passengers?"},{"text":"What would you do if a passenger becomes disruptive?"},{"text":"How would you respond if a passenger ignores a safety instruction?"},{"text":"What does excellent customer service mean in aviation?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cabin crew does not normally require a postgraduate degree for progression."},{"type":"p","text":"However, PG study can help if you want to move into management."},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MBA Aviation Management"},{"text":"MBA Airport Management"},{"text":"MBA Hospitality Management"},{"text":"MBA Tourism Management"},{"text":"MBA Operations"},{"text":"MBA Human Resources"},{"text":"MBA Business Analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Aviation management route"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cabin Crew","Senior Cabin Crew","Supervisor/Purser","MBA/Aviation Management","Cabin/Airline Operations Management"]},{"type":"h","text":"Government/Public-Sector Route"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential aviation-related areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airports"},{"text":"Airport operators"},{"text":"Government aviation organisations"},{"text":"Airport passenger services"},{"text":"Aviation administration"},{"text":"Ground operations"},{"text":"Tourism and aviation bodies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For government or public-sector employment, eligibility depends on the specific recruitment notification. Always verify current age, education, medical and other requirements from the official notification."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential postgraduate fields:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aviation Management"},{"text":"Airline Management"},{"text":"Airport Management"},{"text":"Hospitality Management"},{"text":"Tourism Management"},{"text":"Aviation Operations"},{"text":"International Hospitality"},{"text":"Airline Revenue Management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Countries to consider"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"UAE"},{"text":"Singapore"},{"text":"Switzerland"},{"text":"New Zealand"},{"text":"Netherlands"}]},{"type":"h","text":"International opportunities"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"International Cabin Crew"},{"text":"Senior Cabin Crew"},{"text":"Cabin Supervisor"},{"text":"Cabin Trainer"},{"text":"Aviation Customer Experience Specialist"},{"text":"Airline Operations Executive"},{"text":"Airport Operations Manager"}]},{"type":"p","text":"International employment requires appropriate work authorization and compliance with the airline's recruitment and aviation requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Stage 1 — Entry"},{"type":"h","text":"Cabin Crew Trainee → Cabin Crew"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"},{"text":"Passenger service"},{"text":"Cabin preparation"},{"text":"Teamwork"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 2 — Experienced"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Cabin Crew"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Leading sections of the cabin"},{"text":"Supporting junior crew"},{"text":"Passenger escalation"},{"text":"Service coordination"},{"text":"Safety compliance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 3 — Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"Cabin Supervisor / Purser / Inflight Supervisor"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crew coordination"},{"text":"Safety oversight"},{"text":"Passenger experience"},{"text":"Cabin documentation"},{"text":"Operational decisions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 4 — Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cabin Crew Trainer"},{"text":"Safety Trainer"},{"text":"Cabin Quality Executive"},{"text":"Service Standards Specialist"},{"text":"Crew Resource Management Trainer"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 5 — Management"},{"type":"h","text":"Cabin Services Manager / Cabin Operations Manager"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Crew performance"},{"text":"Training"},{"text":"Service standards"},{"text":"Safety compliance"},{"text":"Scheduling coordination"},{"text":"Quality assurance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 6 — Senior Leadership"},{"type":"p","text":"Head of Cabin Services / Head of Inflight Operations / Senior Airline Operations Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 1 — Cabin Training"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cabin Crew","Senior Cabin Crew","Cabin Trainer","Training Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Safety training"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Crew Resource Management"},{"text":"Instructional design"},{"text":"Assessment"},{"text":"Coaching"},{"text":"Presentation skills"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 2 — Cabin Quality"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cabin Crew","Senior Crew","Quality Executive","Cabin Quality Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Service audits"},{"text":"Safety compliance"},{"text":"SOP adherence"},{"text":"Passenger feedback"},{"text":"Incident analysis"},{"text":"Corrective actions"},{"text":"Performance metrics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 3 — Aviation Operations"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cabin Crew","Senior Crew","Aviation Operations","Operations Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airport operations"},{"text":"Flight operations awareness"},{"text":"Crew coordination"},{"text":"Ground handling"},{"text":"Disruption management"},{"text":"Operational analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This route is particularly useful for cabin crew members who eventually want a land-based management career."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialist Route 4 — Premium & VIP Aviation"},{"type":"flow","items":["Cabin Crew","Premium Cabin Crew","VIP Aviation","Private Aviation Service Manager"]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Luxury hospitality"},{"text":"Personalised service"},{"text":"High-profile passenger handling"},{"text":"Discretion and confidentiality"},{"text":"Fine dining"},{"text":"International etiquette"},{"text":"Premium travel coordination"}]}]},{"heading":"AI & Future of Cabin Crew","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly automate some administrative and routine passenger-service activities, but human safety response, empathy, judgement and physical emergency assistance remain central."},{"type":"h","text":"AI applications"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Predictive passenger assistance"},{"text":"AI translation"},{"text":"Personalised service recommendations"},{"text":"Disruption communication"},{"text":"Crew scheduling optimisation"},{"text":"Predictive maintenance information"},{"text":"Passenger sentiment analysis"},{"text":"Automated service requests"},{"text":"Digital travel assistants"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Future-ready cabin crew"},{"type":"p","text":"The professional will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Safety","Hospitality","Technology","Communication","Cultural Intelligence"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cabin crew does not require programming, but technology literacy is increasingly useful."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airline mobile applications"},{"text":"Passenger service systems"},{"text":"Digital documentation"},{"text":"CRM concepts"},{"text":"Excel basics"},{"text":"Power BI awareness"},{"text":"AI productivity tools"},{"text":"Digital communication"},{"text":"Cybersecurity awareness"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For those moving into management, develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"Operational analytics"}]}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Future aviation may increasingly include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI passenger assistants"},{"text":"Automated biometric processing"},{"text":"Smart cabins"},{"text":"Connected aircraft"},{"text":"Predictive passenger services"},{"text":"Real-time translation"},{"text":"Robotics for selected onboard/ground tasks"},{"text":"Personalised cabin experiences"},{"text":"Data-driven crew scheduling"},{"text":"Sustainable aviation operations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential future roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital Cabin Experience Manager"},{"text":"Cabin AI Operations Specialist"},{"text":"Passenger Experience Strategist"},{"text":"Smart Cabin Operations Manager"},{"text":"Cabin Safety & Technology Manager"},{"text":"Aviation Customer Experience Director"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term professionals will move beyond basic service into safety leadership, passenger experience, training, quality, technology and operations management."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Aviation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Airline operations"},{"text":"Aircraft/cabin awareness"},{"text":"Passenger handling"},{"text":"Safety procedures"},{"text":"Emergency response"},{"text":"Aviation security awareness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Service"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hospitality"},{"text":"Guest relations"},{"text":"Service recovery"},{"text":"Premium service"},{"text":"Cross-cultural communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Safety"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"First Aid"},{"text":"CPR"},{"text":"AED awareness"},{"text":"Fire safety"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spoken English"},{"text":"Presentation"},{"text":"Teamwork"},{"text":"Conflict management"},{"text":"Problem solving"},{"text":"Professional grooming"},{"text":"Stress management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Passenger service systems"},{"text":"Digital airline applications"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI — management advantage"},{"text":"AI productivity tools"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Experience","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–1 year"},{"text":"Cabin Crew Trainee / Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Senior Cabin Crew"}],[{"text":"5–9 years"},{"text":"Cabin Supervisor / Purser"}],[{"text":"8–12 years"},{"text":"Cabin Trainer / Quality / Operations Specialist"}],[{"text":"10–15 years"},{"text":"Cabin Services / Operations Manager"}],[{"text":"15+ years"},{"text":"Head of Cabin Services / Senior Aviation Leadership"}]]},{"type":"p","text":"Progression speed varies significantly by airline, fleet, performance, vacancies and internal promotion structures."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an ideal candidate should have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"BHM/B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration/BTTM"},{"text":"Airline & airport management knowledge"},{"text":"Strong spoken English"},{"text":"Excellent interpersonal skills"},{"text":"Professional grooming and presentation"},{"text":"First Aid/CPR awareness or recognised training"},{"text":"Aviation safety awareness"},{"text":"Passenger-handling experience"},{"text":"Hospitality/airport internship"},{"text":"Strong customer-service capability"},{"text":"Conflict-resolution skills"},{"text":"Cross-cultural awareness"},{"text":"Teamwork and leadership experience"},{"text":"Airline interview preparation"},{"text":"Awareness of current airline-specific eligibility requirements"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal Profile"},{"type":"p","text":"BHM/B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration/BTTM + Airline & Airport Management + aviation/hospitality internship + strong communication + safety & first-aid knowledge + passenger handling + professional grooming + service excellence + cross-cultural skills → Cabin Crew → Senior Cabin Crew → Purser/Cabin Supervisor → Cabin Trainer/Quality/Operations → Cabin Services Manager → Head of Cabin Services."},{"type":"p","text":"1368 | BHM / B.Sc Hospitality & Hotel Administration / BTTM | Airline & Airport Management | Ground Staff"}]}]}